# AI Agent Instructions (Cursor)

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root first: its `bmad:context` block carries the verified
policy, gates, and pitfalls every tool must follow, and the rest of the file carries the
Dream-first workflow and tier model. `.cursor/rules/specs.mdc` is the always-on summary.

`CLAUDE.md` carries Claude Code-only notes; skip it. The conda-forge-expert lifecycle, the
BMAD project switch and the PR CI gates are in `AGENTS.md`; the skill reference and the rest
of what `CLAUDE.md` used to carry are in `docs/reference/agent-instruction-notes.md`
(`AGENTS.md` § *Read on trigger* says when to read it).
Write your own working output under `.cursor/`, never into a Tier-3 planning dir.
